130
00:04:27,340 --> 00:04:28,560
Time to go full throttle.

131
00:04:30,400 --> 00:04:31,580
Hey, no fair!

132
00:04:33,800 --> 00:04:35,580
Moisting Force Megamite Power!

133
00:04:35,880 --> 00:04:38,460
I gotta direct all my mojo into my wings!

134
00:04:38,620 --> 00:04:40,740
Ew!

135
00:04:41,160 --> 00:04:42,660
Oh my god, it's the pain!

136
00:04:42,840 --> 00:04:43,680
My port flappers!

137
00:04:43,940 --> 00:04:44,860
Come on, Restarté!

138
00:04:44,940 --> 00:04:45,960
You gotta dig deep!

139
00:04:46,240 --> 00:04:47,060
You can do it!

140
00:04:47,080 --> 00:04:48,560
Put your wings into it!

141
00:04:50,780 --> 00:04:53,240
Looks like special measures of the divine realm

142
00:04:53,240 --> 00:04:54,560
aren't so special, huh?

143
00:04:57,600 --> 00:04:59,760
Such a princess, honestly.

144
00:05:00,680 --> 00:05:02,300
Come on, let's go.

145
00:05:02,300 --> 00:05:02,740
Huh?

146
00:05:08,620 --> 00:05:10,860
Wow, he's such a gentleman.

147
00:05:11,340 --> 00:05:12,720
He's even holding my hand.

148
00:05:12,980 --> 00:05:14,360
It feels like we're on a date.

149
00:05:14,420 --> 00:05:14,960
Hey, Rista.

150
00:05:15,200 --> 00:05:16,520
Yes, what is it?

151
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:17,580
My name?

152
00:05:17,980 --> 00:05:19,980
Not the usual hey or hey you.

153
00:05:20,680 --> 00:05:21,540
Oh, you rascal.

154
00:05:22,120 --> 00:05:23,500
Inner celestial love is forbidden.

155
00:05:23,500 --> 00:05:25,180
But I won't tell if you won't.

156
00:05:25,960 --> 00:05:26,400
Wait.

157
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:28,520
We could totally be making out right now.

158
00:05:28,920 --> 00:05:29,720
What the crap?

159
00:05:29,800 --> 00:05:31,060
I'm just gonna go for it.

160
00:05:31,060 --> 00:05:32,440
I think we need to speed it up.

161
00:05:32,660 --> 00:05:32,960
What?

162
00:05:32,960 --> 00:05:50,440
I thought it was a goner.

163
00:05:50,640 --> 00:05:52,280
You always forget that you're immortal.

164
00:05:52,740 --> 00:05:53,400
Funny, though.

165
00:05:53,580 --> 00:05:54,820
You sure look dead to me.

166
00:05:55,160 --> 00:05:56,820
And whose fault do you think that is?

167
00:05:56,820 --> 00:05:59,100
I've got both butts on my beautiful wings.

168
00:05:59,140 --> 00:06:00,460
I look like I've been molting.

169
00:06:00,480 --> 00:06:02,820
Can't you fix them with your fancy pants healing magic?

170
00:06:03,400 --> 00:06:04,840
Anyway, shut your face, Hole.

171
00:06:05,180 --> 00:06:07,220
We don't want any unexpected company.

172
00:06:08,140 --> 00:06:15,420
So they're marching as one to show the Demon Lord's power.

173
00:06:15,880 --> 00:06:16,800
It's kind of impressive.

174
00:06:17,120 --> 00:06:20,080
So to be on the safe side, I'll break them up before they get too far.

175
00:06:20,660 --> 00:06:22,240
They won't survive my bombardment.

176
00:06:22,720 --> 00:06:23,820
From what bombs, though?

177
00:06:24,080 --> 00:06:26,540
Rockets and missiles don't exist in Gaea Brande.

178
00:06:26,740 --> 00:06:28,880
Good thing I've learned a skill to replace them.

179
00:06:29,020 --> 00:06:29,320
Huh?

180
00:06:29,320 --> 00:06:30,680
With what exactly?

181
00:06:31,420 --> 00:06:32,940
Hush, and I'll show you.

182
00:06:32,960 --> 00:06:36,780
What the...

183
00:06:36,780 --> 00:06:37,940
You're kidding me!

184
00:06:38,380 --> 00:06:40,520
Who hurt you?

185
00:06:41,140 --> 00:06:42,440
The meteor strike.

186
00:06:42,720 --> 00:06:47,700
It's on the smaller side, but if it falls at a sufficiently high speed, the collision will be catastrophic.

187
00:06:48,420 --> 00:06:49,720
Pure annihilation.

188
00:06:49,720 --> 00:06:55,280
I kicked up the energy towards the end.

189
00:06:55,280 --> 00:06:59,300
I kicked up the energy towards the end.

190
00:06:59,300 --> 00:07:04,300
The moment it made impact, it became superheated and vaporized, resulting in an explosion.

191
00:07:04,300 --> 00:07:05,780
Of course, yeah.

192
00:07:05,780 --> 00:07:10,440
Oh, although it's very powerful, it's still a technique with considerable limits.

193
00:07:10,440 --> 00:07:13,440
I can only use it in the open, and it takes a while to cast.

194
00:07:13,440 --> 00:07:16,260
So, at what point did I miss you learning to apocalypse?

195
00:07:16,260 --> 00:07:21,080
When I was in the divine realm, while making poop skirt cry.

196
00:07:21,080 --> 00:07:26,760
Of course, how could I forget you were supposed to be studying sword moves, not torturing the guy.

197
00:07:26,760 --> 00:07:29,640
Well, I think that took out most of them, but I'm not done.

198
00:07:30,120 --> 00:07:32,160
Not until I launch another meteor first.

199
00:07:32,420 --> 00:07:32,860
Awesome.

200
00:07:33,440 --> 00:07:34,500
Talk about gains.

201
00:07:34,840 --> 00:07:38,140
That's strong enough to take out a heavenly king like Deathmogla for sure.

202
00:07:38,860 --> 00:07:40,700
Nothing against Mash and Elulu.

203
00:07:40,700 --> 00:07:43,600
But this boy can do bad all by himself.

204
00:07:44,140 --> 00:07:48,340
All he has to do is make that happen at the Demon Lord's castle, and then our job is done.

205
00:07:48,620 --> 00:07:49,700
Piece of cake.

206
00:07:53,900 --> 00:07:56,760
What happened? Are you all right?

207
00:07:57,280 --> 00:07:58,800
I may have gone too hardcore.

208
00:07:59,380 --> 00:08:00,920
I need to recover for a while.

209
00:08:01,700 --> 00:08:02,460
I got you, hero.

210
00:08:02,860 --> 00:08:05,200
Let's head back to town and get you to the inn right away.

211
00:08:06,380 --> 00:08:08,620
He fired off two of those spells in a row.

212
00:08:08,620 --> 00:08:11,080
I must have eaten up most of his MP.

213
00:08:12,820 --> 00:08:15,280
I started out with 15,000 MP.

214
00:08:16,080 --> 00:08:17,840
There's just 13,000 left.

215
00:08:18,140 --> 00:08:18,500
Huh?

216
00:08:18,740 --> 00:08:21,740
You barely used any of it, you hoarder!

217
00:08:36,040 --> 00:08:37,540
Mash disappeared on you?

218
00:08:37,540 --> 00:08:41,420
Yes. He went missing two days ago, and I still can't find him anywhere.

219
00:08:41,640 --> 00:08:43,480
Maybe he went back home to your village.

220
00:08:43,600 --> 00:08:45,820
That's what worries me. He would have told me first.

221
00:08:45,860 --> 00:08:47,260
I'm sure he's doing fine.

222
00:08:47,380 --> 00:08:50,120
The chances are slim to none that he'll run into any real trouble.

223
00:08:50,380 --> 00:08:52,520
Especially now that the undead baddies are gone.

224
00:08:53,120 --> 00:08:55,420
It's because of that hero. Isn't he cool?

225
00:08:55,740 --> 00:08:57,000
I wouldn't go that far.

226
00:08:57,420 --> 00:09:00,140
He won't stop nerding out over this new synthesis skill.

227
00:09:00,580 --> 00:09:02,860
He's spent his reward on new weapons and armor.

228
00:09:02,860 --> 00:09:04,140
And now he's a shut-in.

229
00:09:04,280 --> 00:09:06,320
He's probably tinkering away in his quarters.

230
00:09:06,660 --> 00:09:08,440
Let's strap by and see what he's up to.

231
00:09:11,680 --> 00:09:13,140
Sayah! I'm coming in!

232
00:09:13,860 --> 00:09:15,180
What is this mess?

233
00:09:15,260 --> 00:09:15,600
Rista.

234
00:09:17,820 --> 00:09:19,100
Come check this out.

235
00:09:19,800 --> 00:09:21,440
A platinum sword!

236
00:09:22,320 --> 00:09:23,280
That's amazing!

237
00:09:23,280 --> 00:09:24,940
What'd you do to make this thing?

238
00:09:25,560 --> 00:09:28,500
Combining swords on their own didn't improve their strength by much.

239
00:09:28,780 --> 00:09:31,260
To forge a mighty weapon, I needed something unique.

240
00:09:32,620 --> 00:09:35,340
And then, I found a special catalyst.

241
00:09:35,580 --> 00:09:36,800
So what did you use?

242
00:09:38,140 --> 00:09:39,320
Blonde goddess hair.

243
00:09:40,120 --> 00:09:40,380
What?

244
00:09:41,280 --> 00:09:44,800
I found some in your room, because you shed like an old dying dog.

245
00:09:45,140 --> 00:09:48,160
A little this, a little synthesizing it with a steel blade.

246
00:09:49,520 --> 00:09:51,040
And boom, you're welcome.

247
00:09:51,040 --> 00:09:53,040
Wow. A lot of questions right now.

248
00:09:53,220 --> 00:09:55,340
But I'm glad you found some part of me so useful.

249
00:09:55,800 --> 00:09:56,820
Hold on to that for me.

250
00:09:57,080 --> 00:09:58,140
Also, I need more hair.

251
00:09:58,420 --> 00:09:59,020
Like a lot.

252
00:09:59,340 --> 00:10:00,320
You can borrow my razor.

253
00:10:00,660 --> 00:10:01,780
Do not use the sword.

254
00:10:01,960 --> 00:10:02,720
Shut up!

255
00:10:04,100 --> 00:10:06,440
I've got a special delivery for a hero.

256
00:10:07,300 --> 00:10:07,980
What is that?

257
00:10:08,420 --> 00:10:09,180
